-- ============================================================================
-- DR12 EXPERT DEEP SEED: Well Cost & Time, advanced tier.
-- THIS SEED COMPLETES THE TWELVE-COURSE DRILLING & COMPLETIONS MODULE.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions. The structure row is GENERATED from
-- the tier's manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE CURVE AND THE RISK. What a single number hides. A
-- curve hides its shape, a percentage hides its percentile, and a base case
-- hides where it sits in its own distribution.
--
-- THE IDENTITY, AND IT HOLDS EXACTLY. The final point of the cost-time curve
-- equals the AFE BASE cost, absolute error ZERO under strict equality, across
-- every combination of non-productive and contingency fraction tested. So
-- contingency does NOT accrue along the curve and every total-minus-curve gap
-- IS the contingency. Read down a contingency column the endpoint does not
-- move at all; read across non-productive rows it does, because elapsed days
-- drive the per-day lines. An exact identity is a gift to a reader: it is a
-- one-line audit of a spreadsheet somebody else built.
--
-- WHY YOU HAVE TO SAMPLE. Drilling time goes as one over rate, so cost is
-- CONVEX in rate of penetration and a symmetric range of rates gives an
-- asymmetric range of costs: a window of plus or minus 5 metres an hour around
-- 15 costs 50 hours on the downside and saves only 25 on the upside, exactly
-- double. The consequence is the one that matters: a deterministic estimate
-- built on most-likely rates is NOT a most-likely cost. It is optimistic,
-- structurally, before anybody has been careless. On the capstone well the
-- deterministic base sits at the 16.7th percentile, an 83 percent chance of
-- overrun before contingency.
--
-- A DISTINCTION THE TIER IS CAREFUL ABOUT. The published Monte Carlo fixture's
-- two percent gap between its modal base and its analytic mean is INPUT SKEW,
-- not convexity: that fixture is linear in all four of its uncertainties,
-- which is exactly why it can publish closed-form moments at all. Convexity is
-- demonstrated separately, off the rate sweep. A course that blurred the two
-- would be teaching a right conclusion from a wrong reason.
--
-- AND THE CONVENTION TRAP. The petroleum convention and the cost convention
-- run OPPOSITE ways. The canonical sampler returns the petroleum one, so the
-- field named p90 holds the CHEAP outcome when costs are pushed through it. A
-- reader who takes a cost P90 as a low case has the answer exactly backwards.
-- Every percentile in this tier is labelled with the convention it is in.
--
-- The engine imports ONE shared Monte Carlo module rather than carrying its
-- own, which is the project's single-implementation rule, and a sampled result
-- is only reproducible if the seed is recorded.
-- ============================================================================

values ('wellcost', 'advanced', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-the-cost-time-curve","title":"The Cost Time Curve","lesson_keys":["l01-what-the-curve-shows","l02-how-it-is-built","l03-reading-a-checkpoint","l04-the-curve-against-the-plan"]},{"key":"m02-the-endpoint-identity","title":"The Endpoint Identity","lesson_keys":["l01-where-the-curve-ends","l02-contingency-does-not-accrue","l03-why-that-is-the-right-choice","l04-an-identity-worth-checking"]},{"key":"m03-uncertainty","title":"Uncertainty","lesson_keys":["l01-what-actually-varies","l02-rate-of-penetration-dominates","l03-choosing-a-distribution","l04-correlation","l05-the-canonical-sampler"]},{"key":"m04-why-convexity-bites","title":"Why Convexity Bites","lesson_keys":["l01-time-goes-as-one-over-rate","l02-the-mean-moves-up","l03-no-closed-form-to-fall-back-on","l04-why-you-have-to-sample","l05-a-seed-is-part-of-the-answer"]},{"key":"m05-reading-a-risked-result","title":"Reading a Risked Result","lesson_keys":["l01-percentiles","l02-the-convention-trap","l03-where-the-base-case-sits","l04-what-a-contingency-percentage-buys","l05-what-the-risked-run-cannot-tell-you"]},{"key":"m06-the-expert-reading","title":"The Expert Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
